Feature parity with the legacy Enyo phone app (com.palm.app.phone)
=================================================================

The legacy app's own source was never open sourced; what is ported here was
reconstructed from the copy in core-apps/com.palm.app.phone. Ported code carries
a comment naming the legacy file it came from.


Ported
------

* Dial string handling (source/telephonydialhandler/)
    * emergency numbers, from oFono with the standard fallback list
    * emergency dialling with the radio off: power up, wait for registration, redial
    * MMI codes -- call forwarding, call waiting, call barring, CLIR/CLIP/CNAP,
      IMEI, PIN/PUK change -- carried out over the matching oFono interfaces
    * USSD, including interactive sessions the user can reply to
    * CLIR prefixes (*31# / #31#)
    * in-call control digits (3GPP 22.030: 0, 1, 2, 3, 1X, 2X)
    * post-dial strings: ',' pauses and sends, ';' waits for the user
    * launch codes (#*NNN#) that hand off to another application
* Call management
    * several calls at once: hold, swap, merge into a conference, split back out
    * add a second call from the in-call screen
    * call waiting, announced with the short tone instead of the ringtone
    * popupalert window for incoming calls (was already there)
    * missed-call notification and alert with "Call back"
    * "unable to connect" alert, with a "Turn radio on" action in airplane mode
    * audio routing: earpiece, speaker, wired headset, bluetooth; speaker while
      docked on a Touchstone; proximity sensor while held to the ear
* Phone number formatting against the current region, on the dialpad as you type
  and everywhere a number is displayed
* Contact lookup: search by name or number, pick which number to call
* Type-ahead contact match on the dialpad
* Favourites: display name, photo, and one row per number
* Call history: swipe to delete, clear all from the app menu, call back, text,
  add to / view in Contacts, filter by name or number
* Voicemail: mailbox number from the SIM, long press on 1, app menu entry,
  new-message notification
* Dialing shortcuts (a prefix per number length)
* SIM PIN and PUK, with the full PUK -> new PIN -> confirm sequence
* Emergency dialpad over a locked SIM
* Preferences: call forwarding, call waiting, caller ID, call barring, voicemail
  number, dialing shortcuts, SIM PIN
* Launch actions from other applications (dial, answer, reject, swap, merge,
  extract, dtmf, activecall, voicemail, calllog, favorites, dialpad)
* App menu
* Synergy: calling over any account, not just the modem
    * transport registry built from PHONE-capable accounts + com.palm.callcapabilities:1
    * connector calls driven over the account's own luna service and adapted to
      look like ordinary voice calls, so hold/swap/merge/DTMF/history all apply
    * dial proxy: preferred service per domestic/international call, and a
      dial-time chooser when the user has expressed no preference
    * per-contact call options -- their numbers and their IM addresses, each
      labelled with the service it goes over
    * Video tab, shown only when a signed-in account supports video
    * buddy presence from com.palm.imbuddystatus:1
    * call log records and reuses the account each call went over
    * "Your phone accounts" screen
  SERVICE-AGNOSTIC throughout: no connector is named anywhere in the app, so a
  new one needs an account template and no code.
* Visuals matched to the webOS 3.x phone app as it runs on the TouchPad:
  charcoal chrome, top tab bar with icon + label, light contact lists with the
  service in grey caps on the right, and the black call card with one line per
  call


Deliberately not ported
-----------------------

* CDMA-era features: OTASP, MSL, PRL, provisioning, world phone / multimode.
  oFono has no equivalent and the hardware is gone.
* Skype specifically: its backend is gone. Any other connector that declares a
  PHONE capability is supported without naming it.
* Visual voicemail: carrier-specific, needs a VVM service that LuneOS lacks.
* Voice dialing: needs a speech recognition engine.
* First-launch / account setup screens.


Still missing
-------------

* Call history needs proper support in webos-telephonyd for calls placed while
  the app is not running.
* Extracting person:1 data for favourites still reads the raw db8 record rather
  than going through a contacts service.
* Bluetooth handsfree: the audio route is detected, but AT command handling
  (answering from the headset) relies on the launch-action path rather than a
  direct oFono Handsfree binding.
* Fixed dialing (FDN) is reported by oFono but there is no UI for editing the
  FDN list.
* Network operator selection has no UI.
